From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lukasz Sobala <lsobala1@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 03:13:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] aic8800: fix building on 7.2 kernels

Two more changes in 7.2 break the vendor driver:

 - strncpy() is gone; the declaration went out of linux/string.h and
   the implementation out of lib/string.c. The driver has two uses, and
   they want different things:

     rwnx_msg_tx.c copies into a fixed 64-byte firmware message field
     that is not NUL-terminated, which is the padding copy - spelled
     out here as memcpy_and_pad().

     rwnx_platform.c copies a known-length run out of the middle of a
     longer string and writes the terminator itself on the next line,
     so strncpy() never reached a NUL and never padded. That is a
     memcpy().

   Neither replacement needs a version guard: both have been in
   linux/string.h since well before 7.0.

 - The remain_on_channel cfg80211 op takes a trailing const u8 *rx_addr,
   an optional receive address filter for the off-channel period.
   cfg80211 rejects a non-NULL one unless the driver advertises
   NL80211_EXT_FEATURE_ROC_ADDR_FILTER, which this driver does not, so
   it is always NULL here and ignoring it matches what mac80211 does
   with it. Guarded on LINUX_VERSION_CODE, so 7.0 (edge) is unaffected.

Signed-off-by: Lukasz Sobala <lsobala1@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/aicsemi/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_main.c b/drivers/net/wireless/aicsemi/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_main.c
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/aicsemi/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/aicsemi/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_main.c
@@ -5228,7 +5228,18 @@
 static int
 rwnx_cfg80211_remain_on_channel(struct wiphy *wiphy, struct wireless_dev *wdev,
 								struct ieee80211_channel *chan,
-								unsigned int duration, u64 *cookie)
+								unsigned int duration, u64 *cookie
+#if LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(7, 2, 0)
+								/*
+								 * 7.2 added an optional receive address filter for the
+								 * off-channel period. cfg80211 refuses a non-NULL one
+								 * unless the driver sets NL80211_EXT_FEATURE_ROC_ADDR_FILTER,
+								 * which this one does not, so it is always NULL here.
+								 * mac80211 ignores it in the same way.
+								 */
+								, const u8 *rx_addr
+#endif
+								)
 {
 	return rwnx_cfg80211_remain_on_channel_(wiphy, wdev, chan, duration, cookie, false);
 }
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/aicsemi/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_msg_tx.c b/drivers/net/wireless/aicsemi/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_msg_tx.c
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/aicsemi/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_msg_tx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/aicsemi/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_msg_tx.c
@@ -3428,7 +3428,13 @@
 		return -ENOMEM;
 
 	/* Set parameters for the MM_DBG_TRIGGER_REQ message */
-	strncpy(req->error, msg, sizeof(req->error));
+	/*
+	 * strncpy() is gone in 7.2. req->error is a fixed 64-byte field of a
+	 * firmware message and is not NUL-terminated, so spell out what
+	 * strncpy() did: copy at most the field size, pad the rest.
+	 */
+	memcpy_and_pad(req->error, sizeof(req->error), msg,
+				   strnlen(msg, sizeof(req->error)), '\0');
 
 	/* Send the MM_DBG_TRIGGER_REQ message to LMAC FW */
 	return rwnx_send_msg(rwnx_hw, req, 0, -1, NULL);
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/aicsemi/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_platform.c b/drivers/net/wireless/aicsemi/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_platform.c
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/aicsemi/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_platform.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/aicsemi/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_platform.c
@@ -727,7 +727,12 @@
 		p--;
 
 	p++;
-	strncpy(val, dst, p -dst);
+	/*
+	 * strncpy() is gone in 7.2. dst..p is a known-length run inside a longer
+	 * string, so strncpy() never reached its NUL and never padded; the
+	 * terminator is the line below. That is a plain memcpy().
+	 */
+	memcpy(val, dst, p - dst);
 	val[p - dst] = 0;
 	return 0;
 }
